    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Who is Hawk Host best for?</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-300 mb-4">Hawk Host is genuinely strong for one niche: Asia-Pacific buyers who want a sub-$30/mo KVM VPS with a nearby datacenter. The combination of Singapore + Hong Kong locations at this price tier is rare outside of Vultr and DigitalOcean, which cost 2-3x more for the same RAM tier.</p>
    <p class="text-gray-300 mb-4">It is also a good choice for US-based developers who want a long-running, stable budget host with a 60-day money-back window to test under real workloads. The lack of GPU tiers is the clearest gap — for AI inference workloads specifically, look at our <a href="/blog/cheap-vps-local-llm-inference-2026/" class="text-orange-500 hover:text-orange-400">CPU inference comparison</a> for the better-fit hosts.</p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Hawk Host vs alternatives</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-300 mb-4">At the $5 entry tier Hawk Host directly competes with the <a href="https://my.racknerd.com/aff.php?aff=16299" class="text-orange-500 hover:text-orange-400">RackNerd $1.99/mo</a> baseline — RackNerd wins on absolute lowest floor. Hawk Host wins if you specifically need Toronto, Singapore, or Hong Kong at $5/mo where RackNerd's lowest tier is geographically limited.</p>

    <div class="bg-white/5 border border-white/10 rounded-lg p-6 mt-8">
      <p class="text-white font-semibold mb-2">Bottom line</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-300 mb-4">Hawk Host is a reliable 4.0/5 budget VPS with rare Asia-Pacific coverage at the $5-$20 tier. For Asia-Pacific buyers it's a strong pick. For US buyers who don't need that coverage, the <a href="https://my.racknerd.com/aff.php?aff=16299" class="text-orange-500 hover:text-orange-400">RackNerd 12 GB Mega</a> at $19.99/mo offers more RAM for less.</p>
